From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Suno <engineering@projectSuno.org>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] SunoUI: Apps › Display over other apps; an app's On screen
 group

What apps may draw outside their windows (layer-shell surfaces, Mutter
0043-0045, Shell 0380), as the Shell's org.projectSuno.LayerShell1 reports
it on org.gnome.Shell (/org/projectSuno/LayerShell). A new adapter, "layer",
reads Apps, Surfaces and OverlayApps (again on PropertiesChanged, Used and
Clamped) into CFLAYER; its one key, "layerCap", calls SetCapability, which
stores the choice in the permission store (table "Suno", entry
"display-over-apps") and hands it to Mutter at once. Without the Shell, or a
Shell without the interface, CFLAYER is null and nothing below is drawn.

An app's page gets an On screen group above Allowed to: Display over other
apps, Add a panel, Desktop background and Take the keyboard, each a 30 px
glyph tile (layers-2, panel-top, image, keyboard) and a switch, its usage
after the description ("Used today", "Used 3 days ago", "Never used"). The
usage and the tile are violet (SunoUI token "overlay", #b28fef, its soft
fill at 18%) only while the capability is in use now. A note under the group
says what no app can do. Host apps have background and panel unless refused;
sandboxed apps nothing until allowed, as the Shell decides.

Desktop background replaces the "Change wallpaper" row and Take the keyboard
the "Keyboard shortcuts" row: one switch each. Switching one calls
SetCapability and writes the older entry the same way: the wallpaper
portal's (table and entry "wallpaper", the app's Flatpak ID, "yes"/"no",
sandboxed apps only) and GNOME Shell's shortcut inhibitor (table "gnome",
entry "shortcuts-inhibitor", the desktop-file ID, "GRANTED"/"DENIED"). A
switch shows on when either entry allows it, so a grant made earlier through
the portal or GNOME's dialog is shown and is turned off by the same switch.
The old rows are left out only while the On screen group is drawn.

Apps lists Display over other apps ("Apps that can draw above everything"),
a page (overlay-apps) with "N apps allowed · M showing now", an Allowed group
(violet dot; each app's icon, name, usage, a violet "· Showing now" while
its overlay is on screen, a switch) and a Not allowed group: only apps that
asked and were refused ("Asked yesterday"); apps that never asked are not
listed. A switch moves no row while the page is shown. Switches call
SetCapability(app, 4, allowed). The Shell's Overlay settings link opens it:
launch-panel ('applications', ['overlay-apps']), as does
`gnome-control-center applications overlay-apps`. Phone and TV draw the same pages in their
own layouts; there the usage shares the description's wrapping line, and on
a TV the violet dot goes into the indented heading.

The glyphs are Prairie's (SunoUI-layers-2 and SunoUI-panel-top, platform
1.Suno.153). Fixtures may name a
"version" and Suno-v4-* artwork for an app (CFAPPINFO). Test:
Suno-settings-layer-shell (usage words, the list's filtering, and switches
against a stand-in Shell and permission store on a private bus).
---
